# Cargo / Rust build artefacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
Cargo.lock.bak

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Local agent / IDE configuration — these are per-developer, not shared
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Local working data: sample corpora, VT/extraction caches, ad-hoc dumps.
# `data/` contains downloaded malicious samples, VT reports and the
# extraction cache; it must never be pushed to a public remote.
# The directory itself is ignored — even an empty marker like `.gitkeep`
# under data/ would be tracked, so we ignore the whole tree.
data/
# `data-clean/` is the same shape as `data/` but populated from the
# `vt download --clean` benign-corpus query. Same exclusion rationale:
# downloaded VT samples + reports must never be pushed.
data-clean/

# Cross-LLM FP-triage analysis artefacts. Generated by
# `scripts/fp_triage.sh` against `data-clean/`; reproducible from the
# scripts checked in. Outputs are large (multi-MB JSONL/JSON), per-run
# timestamped, and contain LLM provider responses. Ignored to keep the
# repo lean and to avoid leaking any per-tenant model output.
fp-triage*.jsonl
fp-triage*.tsv
results-clean*.json

# Local presentation/demo material (slides, screenshots, recordings) kept
# out of the public repo for the same reason as `data/` — per-author
# artefacts, not part of the shipping codebase.
presentation/

# Local cargo config (often used to point at vendored deps / private mirrors)
.cargo/config.toml

# Pre-commit local cache
.pre-commit-cache/

# Local benchmark caches (multi-LLM scorer caches per-author API state).
benchmarks/.multi-llm-cache*
